      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A refurbishment opportunity with additional site potential subject to P.P on circa 0.46 acres\" \r\n \r\nAshville is an attractive detached period residence, superbly positioned on the much sought-after Thormanby Road just above Howth village.  \r\n\r\nOccupying a generous site of c.0.46 acres with substantial gardens to the front, the property offers an exciting opportunity for those seeking to create a truly special home in one of Dublin’s most desirable coastal locations. \r\n\r\nThe generous site also presents obvious potential for further development, subject to the necessary planning permission. \r\n\r\nThere are two vehicular entrances to access the property, please note there is a right of way in place for the neighbouring property for access from the right hand side entrance.\r\n \r\nThe property requires complete refurbishment, but retains a good deal of its original period features along with an abundance of character and charm. \r\n\r\nAshville offers obvious potential to be transformed into a special family home, combining its period charm with the comforts and style of modern living.\r\n \r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a porch leading into a spacious hall with two generously proportioned reception rooms positioned on either side. To the rear, an inner hallway provides access to a cloakroom and small storage cupboard. There is a large dining room with access to the rear of the property, while the kitchen is positioned to the opposite side and benefits from an adjoining storeroom and a separate utility room.\r\n \r\nUpstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms and a main bathroom.\r\n \r\nTo the rear of the property lies a particularly attractive private, south-facing walled garden, providing a sheltered outdoor space with excellent potential to create a private garden with an ideal aspect. \r\n\r\nThe convenient location is one of Ashville’s greatest attractions. Situated on the favoured Thormanby Road, the property is ideally positioned equidistant between Howth Summit and Howth Village and Harbour, allowing residents to enjoy the very best that the peninsula has to offer.\r\n \r\nThe area is renowned for its spectacular coastal scenery and extensive network of cliff and coastal walks, while the vibrant village and harbour are just minutes away. Here, a wonderful selection of cafés, restaurants, gastro pubs and local amenities provide an enviable lifestyle throughout the year.\r\n \r\nFamilies are particularly well catered for, with an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools in the surrounding area, together with an extensive range of sporting, recreational and community clubs.\r\n \r\nAshville represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial detached period property in an exceptional Howth location, with the scope to create a remarkable family home and, subject to planning, explore the considerable potential offered by its generous site for an additional new home."
      },
